#: ../../../workspace/nexus-build-system-20261012/docs/delivery/soc-extensions-verification.md:95
msgid ""
"H743 DMA borrows request and payload storage until acquire-observed SETTLED."
" Cache-enabled transfers require the caller to own complete aligned cache "
"lines; the provider does not round maintenance outward into neighboring "
"allocations or allocate a bounce buffer. Cancellation and timeout do not "
"revoke the borrow. Failure to withdraw hardware references retains storage "
"in quarantine."
msgstr ""
"H743 DMA borrows request and payload storage until acquire-observed SETTLED."
" Cache-enabled transfers require the caller to own complete aligned cache "
"lines; the provider does not round maintenance outward into neighboring "
"allocations or allocate a bounce buffer. Cancellation and timeout do not "
"revoke the borrow. Failure to withdraw hardware references retains storage "
"in quarantine."

#: ../../../workspace/nexus-build-system-20261012/docs/delivery/soc-extensions-verification.md:101
msgid ""
"The U575 reference admits a fixed TZEN=1 boot profile and an immutable "
"unprivileged NonSecure thread without NonSecure interrupts, an RTOS or "
"concurrent DMA. It clears and verifies future NonSecure RAM before changing "
"attribution, checks final protection state, and enters through the actual "
"compiler CMSE sequence. Its synchronous gateway copies bounded input and "
"checks output before publication. This does not implement general "
"asynchronous cross-domain loans, arbitrary userspace tasks, product "
"authentication or secure update policy. See the [complete "
"contract](../design/u575-trustzone-contract.md)."
msgstr ""
"The U575 reference admits a fixed TZEN=1 boot profile and an immutable "
"unprivileged NonSecure thread without NonSecure interrupts, an RTOS or "
"concurrent DMA. It clears and verifies future NonSecure RAM before changing "
"attribution, checks final protection state, and enters through the actual "
"compiler CMSE sequence. Its synchronous gateway copies bounded input and "
"checks output before publication. This does not implement general "
"asynchronous cross-domain loans, arbitrary userspace tasks, product "
"authentication or secure update policy. See the [complete "
"contract](../design/u575-trustzone-contract.md)."

#: ../../../workspace/nexus-build-system-20261012/docs/delivery/soc-extensions-verification.md:110
msgid "Evidence rules"
msgstr "Evidence rules"

#: ../../../workspace/nexus-build-system-20261012/docs/delivery/soc-extensions-verification.md:112
msgid ""
"Normal commit hooks execute the complete GoogleTest/GoogleMock, "
"configuration and tool suites for behavioral changes. Formal qualification "
"additionally binds a clean canonical commit and tree, actual compiler "
"inputs, raw command output, configuration and linked artifacts. Failed "
"attempts remain failed evidence; changing the source requires new source-"
"bound execution."
msgstr ""
"Normal commit hooks execute the complete GoogleTest/GoogleMock, "
"configuration and tool suites for behavioral changes. Formal qualification "
"additionally binds a clean canonical commit and tree, actual compiler "
"inputs, raw command output, configuration and linked artifacts. Failed "
"attempts remain failed evidence; changing the source requires new source-"
"bound execution."

#: ../../../workspace/nexus-build-system-20261012/docs/delivery/soc-extensions-verification.md:118
msgid ""
"The verification work exposed missing generated-header input in the H743 ARM"
" startup test, a fixed virtual-environment path in CPU configuration tests, "
"an uncontrolled scheduling assumption in a serial-noise test, and lost "
"forced-include context in static analysis. Sanitizer jobs also exposed "
"register-mask width conversions in host models and signal-dependent "
"termination observers. Their regressions retain the actual compiler warnings"
" and production nonreturning loops; test observers must work without a "
"signal-delivery point inside those loops. U575 production clock and MPU "
"masks also required explicit 32-bit operands before bit operations for GCC "
"13 on the LP64 sanitizer host. The independent comparison found identical "
"allocated ARM sections for the tested old/new translation units after "
"normalizing `__FILE__`; this is a scoped code and storage comparison, not "
"measured cycles or a promise for every compiler. Regression evidence and "
"final execution status belong with the delivery index. No suppression or "
"skipped test can substitute for closing these findings."
msgstr ""
"The verification work exposed missing generated-header input in the H743 ARM"
" startup test, a fixed virtual-environment path in CPU configuration tests, "
"an uncontrolled scheduling assumption in a serial-noise test, and lost "
"forced-include context in static analysis. Sanitizer jobs also exposed "
"register-mask width conversions in host models and signal-dependent "
"termination observers. Their regressions retain the actual compiler warnings"
" and production nonreturning loops; test observers must work without a "
"signal-delivery point inside those loops. U575 production clock and MPU "
"masks also required explicit 32-bit operands before bit operations for GCC "
"13 on the LP64 sanitizer host. The independent comparison found identical "
"allocated ARM sections for the tested old/new translation units after "
"normalizing `__FILE__`; this is a scoped code and storage comparison, not "
"measured cycles or a promise for every compiler. Regression evidence and "
"final execution status belong with the delivery index. No suppression or "
"skipped test can substitute for closing these findings."

